146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (The Idea of ShED Forum \(Shershahbadi Educational Dialogue Forum\) emerged when a few Shershahbadi students at Maulana Azad National Urdu University \(MANUU\) realized that students from their community were extremely limited in higher education. This highlighted the distance between the Shershahbadi community and universities.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (Primarily residing in Seemanchal, Bihar, and parts of West Bengal and Jharkhand, the community has long faced educational and socio-economic challenges. Lack of awareness, guidance, exposure, and opportunities often prevented talented and aspiring students from accessing higher education.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (The Forum was envisioned as a bridge connecting students with information, guidance, mentorship, and opportunities. Its core principle was that every student who secures university admission should help at least one more student enter higher education the following year, creating a culture of mentorship and collective responsibility.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
